# Source of truth for the light_dbr19_all umbrella CI job's Python deps
# (classic DBR 19, full feature set).
# Consumed by CI via: pip install --require-hashes -r python/geobrix/requirements-light-dbr19-all-ci.txt
#
# Regenerate (from python/geobrix/):
#   uv pip compile --generate-hashes --python-version 3.12 \
#       --output-file requirements-light-dbr19-all-ci.txt requirements-light-dbr19-all-ci.in
#
# This .in uses a local-package-with-extra reference so uv expands [light_dbr19_all]
# directly from pyproject.toml. The [light_dbr19_all] extra pulls [light_dbr19]+[stac]+[vizx]+[overture].
# [light_dbr19] drops the <2.2 cap on mapbox-vector-tile (resolves to >=2.2, protobuf 6.x;
# classic DBR 19 requires protobuf>=6.31.1 via grpcio-status).
# [light_all] is the Serverless/DBR<=18 twin: see requirements-light-all-ci.in.
#
# Note: CI resolves without Serverless grpcio-status constraints; the protobuf version
# in this lock (6.x) reflects the absence of the <2.2 mvt cap in [light_dbr19]. No
# stac/vizx/overture transitive dep conflicts with protobuf>=6 (verified by uv exit 0).

# Local package — expands geobrix[light_dbr19_all] from pyproject.toml
.[light_dbr19_all]
